  "answer_text": "It looks like you're referencing the **Georgia Motor Vehicle Division (MVD) Tag Renewal website**. Here's a summary of what that page and the broader MVD portal offers:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\ude97 Georgia MVD \u2013 Tag Renewal Portal\n**URL:** [https://mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx](https://mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx)\n\nGeorgia MVD offers online applications and information regarding **tag renewals, license plates, titles, dealer registrations, and commercial vehicles**.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd11 What You Can Do on the Tag Renewal Page:\n- **Renew your vehicle tag/registration online**\n- If the address on your Renewal Notice is **not correct**, do **not** renew online. You must also present your **driver's license or Georgia ID** to renew.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccb Other Key Features of the MVD Portal:\n- You can request services without re-entering VINs, license plates, or driver's license numbers each time, quickly access vehicles associated with your driver's license, and request a **replacement title online**.\n\n- In partnership with County Tax Commissioners, the Department of Revenue\u2013Motor Vehicle Division (MVD) is responsible for issuing **certificates of title, disabled persons' parking permits (placards), certificates of registration, and license plates** to vehicles owned or leased and operated in the State of Georgia.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcde Contact & Verification:\n- The telephone number for MVD is **(855) 406-5221**.\n- Call **1-800-GEORGIA** to verify that a website is an official website of the State of Georgia.\n\n---\n\n### \u26a0\ufe0f Important Note:\nIt appears the **old MVD portal** (`mvd.dor.ga.gov`) may be transitioning to the newer **DRIVES e-Services** platform. You can also access vehicle registration services at: \ud83d\udc49 [https://eservices.drives.ga.gov](https://eservices.drives.ga.gov)\n\nWould you like help with a specific task, such as renewing your tag or finding a tag office?",
